  "preview_mark_about": "M8 step 3 (the preview plan, section 3.1; ADR 0010's revision on previews, item 2). Contract only: nothing writes or reads this form until steps 6 and 8. A preview host's entry is the preview mark, then the access epoch, then a colon, then exactly the form a production entry of that host has: the script's name with or without the code mark, alone on a default host, or followed by the separator and the host on a custom one. The epoch is the preview slot's access epoch when the entry was written, in decimal: 0, or a digit other than 0 followed by at most 14 more digits, so it is exact as a JavaScript number; no sign, no leading zero, no space. The mark and the epoch are taken off once, from the start only, and what is left is read as a production entry of that host is; anything else is not an entry. The content Worker dispatches a preview entry only through the preview namespace binding and an unmarked entry only through the production one, so a production host never reads a preview entry and a preview host never reads a production one. So the vectors cross: every valid preview entry is among the invalid production entries of its host's form (invalid_code_entries, invalid_custom_entries), and every valid production entry among the invalid preview entries of its form, which packages/contracts/check.mjs holds. The host's kind comes from its entry, never its name.",
  "preview_mark": "preview:",
  "preview_epoch_pattern": "^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,14})$",
